## Scope

One `slides` skill replacing text-to-slides and slides-review: a router with `references/make.md` and `references/review.md` (authoring-skills.md router pattern). Author decision "Beamer default": make mode follows `rules/doctype/slides.md`, ODP through LibreOffice conversion; delete the python-pptx/odfpy example references. Slide doctrine lives once, in `rules/doctype/slides.md` (extend it; it is beamer-scoped today); the skill points to it. Keep "never announce success without looking" (render and inspect). Drop the AMAP material and the generic pitch-deck / corporate examples. Description must not collide with the anthropic `pptx` triggers.

Common exit criteria for every child: the body follows `rules/authoring-skills.md` (size, pointer-and-payload split, doctrine in rules and procedure in skills, `model:` pinned on any fan-out, concurrency declared on multi-item steps); no instance-specific material (AMAP talk, one-off scripts); `make skills-catalog` regenerated; `make check-fast`, `make lint`, `make check-agnostic-skills`, `make check-skills-drift` pass; skills resident channel stays under its budget (`tests/test_resident_census.py`). Originals as synced from claude.ai, for reference: the import commit of PR #1075 (8b9691f1) and git history.
